[5] Theorem-facing readout
  THM-571 reconciliation:
    the |14Z cap S|>=7 apex-majority family should be removed from
    the live HYP-2961 counterexample list, modulo the accepted
    below-frontier LRC input used by THM-571.
  Few-apex evidence:
    every structured AP-replacement row with 1<=|14Z cap S|<=6 in this
    qdiv>14 bank has positive exact lift-safe mass, so none is a
    covering zero-open non-migration packet.
    smallest exact lift-safe measure in this run is 563/105105.
    optional exact M fallback displayed minimum 7/89.
  Candidate lemma:
    Fixed-margin few-apex lift theorem.  For primitive qdiv>14 rows
    with at most six multiples of 14, a retained Q/R lift packet has
    positive regular-open Haar mass unless it state-lifts to the K33
    endpoint.  This is the F5/F6 boundary-moment bridge in executable form.
